From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:44:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: keep a queued barrier's resource alive until it is
 emitted

ctx->need_barriers[] holds bare struct zink_resource pointers, but every
counter that decides when an entry goes in or comes out - bind_count,
fb_bind_count, sampler_bind_count - is counted on the zink_resource, which all
the contexts of a screen share. A context that only barriers a resource, in a
blit, a transfer or a readpixels, therefore queues it whenever some other
context of the share group has it bound, and nothing ever removes that entry:
update_img_bind_count() and unbind_fb_surface() remove from the set of the
context that makes the unbind, resource_release() cleans only the context it is
called on, and zink_resource_destroy() runs at screen level with no context at
all. The next draw of the queueing context then reads a freed resource.

A virglrenderer host is exactly that share group - one pipe_context per guest
virgl context, one resource table - and it crashes there. Two guest OpenGL ES
conformance cases reproduce it, KHR-GLES3.packed_depth_stencil.verify_partial_-
attachments.depth24_stencil8 and KHR-GLES3.copy_tex_image_conversions.required.-
texture2d_texture2d, in zink_update_barriers() reading res->obj out of a block
that has already been recycled. An instrumented build that tags every queueing
site and marks a resource dead in zink_resource_destroy() caught twenty such
keys in a single 813-case shard, nine of them queued by
resource_defer_image_barrier() and the rest from sites whose resource address
had since been reused.

Give a queued entry a reference to the resource it names. The owning context
drains its queue on the next draw or dispatch and drops the reference again, so
the resource lives no longer than the barrier that asks for it, and no context
can be left holding a pointer to a resource another context destroyed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c         |   2 +-
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c       | 125 +++++++++++++++---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.h       |   6 +
 .../drivers/zink/zink_synchronization.cpp     |   8 +-
 4 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
